   "daf": "44a",
   "sentenceId": 9,
   "he": "וּמַאֲכִיל בִּתְרוּמָה. דִּכְתִיב: ״וִילִיד בֵּיתוֹ הֵם יֹאכְלוּ בְלַחְמוֹ״, קְרִי בֵיהּ: ״יַאֲכִילוּ בְּלַחְמוֹ״.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches: «And» a one-day-old baby «enables» his mother, an Israelite woman who is no longer married to his father, a priest, to continue «to partake of teruma.» The Gemara explains that this is «as it is written,» with regard to those who are entitled to partake of teruma on account of a priest: «“And those who are born in his house, they may eat [yokhelu] of his bread”» (Leviticus 22:11). «Read into» the verse: Those who are born in his house «enable others to eat [ya’akhilu] of his bread,» i.e., on account of her son the priest, the Israelite mother may continue to partake of teruma even after the death of his father."
  }
 ],
